WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.680
Scott Pilgrim vs. the World was&nbsp;
unleashed on the world in 2010,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.320
thanks to director Edgar Wright. Based on the&nbsp;
graphic novels by Bryan Lee O'Malley, the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:14.080
developed a cult following due to its frenetic&nbsp;
action scenes, bizarre and endearing plot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.120
and its spectacular ensemble cast. Here's what&nbsp;
they've been up to since appearing in the film.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.440
In the end, no other actor&nbsp;
could have played the mumbly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:28.800
self-effacing, insecure Scott Pilgrim as&nbsp;
perfectly as Michael Cera. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.440
Cera had already made a name for himself&nbsp;
in popular comedies like Superbad and cult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.400
television favorites like Arrested Development.&nbsp;
However, Scott Pilgrim also gave Cera a chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.160
to flex his action hero chops during the&nbsp;
sequences when he fights Ramona's evil exes.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:44.800
"Mr. Lee!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.920
You're needed back on set."

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:58.160
Since Scott Pilgrim, Cera has continued working&nbsp;
steadily, appearing in plenty of comedies like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.480
This Is The End, as well as dramas&nbsp;
like Molly's Game and Gloria Bell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:08.000
Cera has also dabbled in voice work, lending his&nbsp;
vocal stylings to the 2021 animated film Cryptozoo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.840
and taking on the role of Robin in The&nbsp;
Lego Batman Movie. On the small screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.840
Cera has also been seen in shows like Wet&nbsp;
Hot American Summer: First Day of Camp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.840
the 2017 Twin Peaks revival — and&nbsp;
of course, the Netflix-produced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.320
continuation of Arrested Development, where&nbsp;
he reprised his role as George Michael Bluth.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:31.120
The role of the intimidatingly beautiful,&nbsp;
smart, and unflappably cool Ramona Flowers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.640
could have been harder to relate to with&nbsp;
the wrong actor in the role, but luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.040
Mary Elizabeth Winstead was more than up to the&nbsp;
task when Edgar Wright tasked her with the part.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.400
Ultimately, despite the colorful absurdity of the&nbsp;
plot, viewers can't help but understand why Scott&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.600
decides he has to risk his life fighting multiple&nbsp;
evil exes in order to win Ramona's heart. Are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:55.200
these two a couple for the ages? Probably not, but&nbsp;
you'll probably end up rooting for them anyway.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.840
Since appearing in Scott Pilgrim, Winstead has&nbsp;
kept busy, landing roles in a string of films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:05.040
that included The Spectacular Now and Swiss&nbsp;
Army Man. She also had an excellent turn in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.760
2016's 10 Cloverfield Lane. In more recent&nbsp;
years, Winstead has appeared in a season of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:16.400
FX's anthology series Fargo and films like 2019's&nbsp;
Gemini Man. Circling back to superhero action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:21.920
Winstead also delivered a supporting turn&nbsp;
as Huntress in 2020's DC hit Birds of Prey.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.800
"They call me… Huntress."

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.560
Scott Pilgrim vs. the World is packed to the&nbsp;
brim with funny characters, but as Scott's dry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.720
quick-witted roommate Wallace, Kieran Culkin&nbsp;
may just deliver the funniest performance in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.200
the entire film. Wallace, who spends the film&nbsp;
making conquests out of several handsome men&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.920
and just generally supporting Scott, always&nbsp;
has the perfect thing to say at just the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.240
time, and it's impossible not to laugh at&nbsp;
Culkin's interpretation of the character.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:55.360
Culkin has been acting since he was a kid, but&nbsp;
HBO subscribers and prestige television fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.600
definitely know him best for his supporting&nbsp;
role as the cocky Roman Roy on Succession,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:03.760
the black comedy about a wealthy family and its&nbsp;
children all jockeying for their father's seat of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.640
power at the head of the family mega-conglomerate.&nbsp;
Culkin earned Emmy nods two years in a row&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:12.960
for the role, proving that his delightful&nbsp;
performance as Roman is no flash in the pan.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.560
As Scott continues his courtship of Ramona,&nbsp;
he's surprised to discover that he must defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.720
her exes in order to earn the privilege&nbsp;
of dating her... and one of those exes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.040
is an actual movie star. When Scott and&nbsp;
Ramona cross paths with her second ex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:31.760
Lucas Lee, played by Chris Evans, he's in the&nbsp;
midst of filming his newest blockbuster film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:35.360
but he still takes the time to&nbsp;
fight Scott for Ramona's affections.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.280
"I used to date that clown." "Aaaaaand…" "ACTION!"

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.440
By the point Evans signed on to play&nbsp;
Lucas Lee in Scott Pilgrim vs. the World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.840
the actor was already a movie star in real&nbsp;
life. After his first comic book adaptation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:53.520
2007's Fantastic Four, Evans took on another&nbsp;
role from Marvel's comics that would eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.520 --> 00:04:00.240
come to define a truly blockbuster chapter in&nbsp;
his career: Steve Rogers, aka Captain America.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:05.200
Evans debuted in the role just one year after&nbsp;
Scott Pilgrim, starring in 2011's Captain America:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:10.640
The First Avenger and reprised it for two more&nbsp;
Captain America films and several Avengers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:16.080
crossover movies before hanging up his shield&nbsp;
for good in 2019's Avengers: Endgame. Beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.760
the Marvel Cinematic Universe, Evans has&nbsp;
also appeared in a handful of other roles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:24.640
including the critically beloved hit Knives Out,&nbsp;
showcasing that he's more than just an Avenger.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.240
As Scott's sister Stacey, Anna Kendrick doesn't&nbsp;
have the biggest role in Scott Pilgrim vs. the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:35.440
World, but it's a delight to see her every time&nbsp;
she pops up onscreen, whether she's scolding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:40.880
Scott over his inappropriately aged girlfriend&nbsp;
or losing yet another boyfriend to Wallace's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:46.080
charms. Stacey serves as one of a few female&nbsp;
characters that seem to make up a Greek chorus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:51.520
that yells at Scott more or less nonstop,&nbsp;
but thanks to Kendrick's natural charm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:56.000
she makes Stacey a fully realized character&nbsp;
in a very short amount of screen time.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.080
"Hey. Yeah, I know. Oh, it's sooooo pathetic."

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.480
Kendrick got even busier in the years&nbsp;
after Scott Pilgrim — by that point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.640
she already had an Academy Award nomination&nbsp;
for Up in the Air, and she followed her early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:13.040
successes with critically acclaimed hits&nbsp;
like 50/50, Pitch Perfect and its sequels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.400
and Into the Woods. The actor has also lent her&nbsp;
voice to 2016's Trolls and its sequel, and she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:23.840
became a published author the same year when she&nbsp;
released a memoir, titled Scrappy Little Nobody.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:28.880
Long before the film begins, Scott has his&nbsp;
heart broken by his own evil ex, who also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:33.840
plays in a band — albeit one that's much more&nbsp;
successful than his own. Played by Brie Larson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:38.400
the lead singer of the Clash at Demonhead,&nbsp;
Natalie "Envy" Adams has, according to Scott,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.720
sold out and signed with a huge label. By&nbsp;
the time the film's narrative gets started,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:47.840
Envy is an enormous star already. However, when&nbsp;
she and Scott reunite and it turns out that her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:53.520
bassist/boyfriend is yet another ex of&nbsp;
Ramona's, the situation gets even stickier.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:58.640
After appearing in indies like 2013's The&nbsp;
Spectacular Now and big blockbuster comedies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:03.360
like Trainwreck, Larson achieved a huge career&nbsp;
milestone when she won an Oscar — as well as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:07.360
several other major awards — for her leading&nbsp;
performance as a kidnapping victim with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:12.960
young son in the gripping 2015 drama Room. In the&nbsp;
aftermath of her Oscar win, Larson started picking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:18.480
up blockbuster roles in films like 2017's Kong:&nbsp;
Skull Island, and in 2019, she made her debut in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:23.680
the Marvel Cinematic Universe as Carol Danvers,&nbsp;
also known as Captain Marvel. Beyond acting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:28.880
Larson has also stepped behind the camera;&nbsp;
in 2017, she made her directorial debut,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:33.840
Unicorn Store, featuring her friend and&nbsp;
Captain Marvel co-star Samuel L. Jackson.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:40.080
Scott's band, Sex Bob-omb, only has one&nbsp;
female member. It's easy to see that Kim Pine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.920
played by Alison Pill, definitely has&nbsp;
enough attitude and talent to balance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:48.800
the band's scales. As Sex Bob-omb's drummer,&nbsp;
Kim is clearly still pretty bitter about an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.040
obviously bad breakup between her and Scott.&nbsp;
Though she can't help herself from making snide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:57.840
comments about Scott more or less constantly,&nbsp;
she still supports him and the band overall.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.680
Pill has appeared in several films&nbsp;
since, like 2013's Snowpiercer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:05.120
but is mostly known for TV work.&nbsp;
She took on a starring role in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:09.680
HBO's Aaron Sorkin drama The Newsroom as&nbsp;
network associate producer Maggie Jordan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.520
staying with the show throughout its run. In&nbsp;
recent years, Pill has shown up in projects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:18.800
like American Horror Story: Cult and on CBS'&nbsp;
Star Trek: Picard, which began its run in 2020.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:24.720
As the sarcastic, foul-mouthed Julie who&nbsp;
constantly pops up where Scott least expects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:30.160
to see her, Aubrey Plaza is a perfect addition&nbsp;
to Scott Pilgrim. Julie is no fan of Scott's,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:33.920
to be sure, but she has connections with&nbsp;
everyone in Toronto, which means Plaza&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:39.280
gets to pop up several times... with a black&nbsp;
bar typically obscuring her profane insults.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:42.240
"I can't even believe I'm saying&nbsp;
this, but Envy Adams would like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:46.240
you all to come backstage." "All&nbsp;
of us?" "Did I F------ stutter?"

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:51.040
Before she appeared in Scott Pilgrim, Plaza was&nbsp;
already a part of the ensemble cast of Parks and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:55.920
Recreation. She played the sharp-tongued&nbsp;
and morbid April Ludgate — later April&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:00.720
Ludgate-Dwyer — until the series ended in&nbsp;
2015, at which point she joined FX's Legion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:06.720
Plaza also appears in several films, often playing&nbsp;
dark and quirky, such as in Ingrid Goes West. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:12.080
continued that run in 2020 with two high-profile&nbsp;
indies, Happiest Season and Black Bear.

00:08:13.506 --> 00:08:17.360
Brandon Routh plays one of Ramona's evil&nbsp;
exes as well as Envy's new boyfriend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:21.920
Todd Ingram. He impacts Scott Pilgrim vs. the&nbsp;
World's story in multiple ways, but there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:26.960
one part of his identity that's more important&nbsp;
than anything else: he's a vegan. Thanks to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:33.120
special diet and ability to maintain it, Todd has&nbsp;
pretty intense powers. Envy even spells it out.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:40.053
"Short answer: being vegan just makes&nbsp;
you better than most people." "Bingo."

00:08:40.053 --> 00:08:44.640
Todd's false cloak of veganism is eventually&nbsp;
removed, but the casting of Routh, known for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:49.360
playing one of the most famous superheroes&nbsp;
of all time, is likely no accident. By the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:54.160
time he appeared as Todd, Routh had already&nbsp;
played Superman in 2006's Superman Returns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:58.240
though he was replaced in the franchise&nbsp;
reboot Man of Steel. Since Scott Pilgrim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:02.160
Routh has appeared in a number of projects,&nbsp;
including returning to his superhero roots on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:07.840
the CW's Arrow and its sister shows as Ray "The&nbsp;
Atom" Palmer. He even got to reprise his role as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:13.840
Superman on the CW in the Arrowverse crossover&nbsp;
Crisis on Infinite Earths from 2019 to 2020.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.720
Scott handily defeats most of&nbsp;
Ramona's evil exes, but her final ex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:23.360
powerful music executive Gideon, played by&nbsp;
Jason Schwartzman, is a little bit harder to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:28.320
crack. As soon as Ramona sees Gideon again, she&nbsp;
falls under his spell — which, as it turns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:32.800
is thanks to a literal microchip Gideon&nbsp;
implanted in her neck — and though Scott&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:38.160
thinks he's lost her forever, he wages one final&nbsp;
boss fight against Gideon to win her freedom.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.080
Schwartzman was already starring in HBO's&nbsp;
detective comedy Bored to Death by the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:46.000
he appeared in Scott Pilgrim vs. the World,&nbsp;
but viewers probably know him best from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:50.640
consistent collaborations with director Wes&nbsp;
Anderson - he's appeared in Moonrise Kingdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:55.520
The Grand Budapest Hotel, and 2021's The&nbsp;
French Dispatch, to name a few. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:59.440
he's also found time for non-Anderson&nbsp;
projects, including Saving Mr. Banks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:03.840
the 2014 drama Big Eyes, and the&nbsp;
2018 Netflix comedy Wine Country.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:08.960
Throughout his battles with the first few&nbsp;
exes, Scott keeps calling them Ramona's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:14.640
evil ex-boyfriends, and never seems to take notice&nbsp;
when Ramona corrects him by saying exes. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:20.960
he soon figures out why; one of her exes, Roxy&nbsp;
Richter, definitely isn't a boyfriend at all, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:26.400
she definitely has a bone to pick with Scott. Roxy&nbsp;
is played by the always hilarious Mae Whitman.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:34.401
"I was just a little bicurious."&nbsp;
"Well honey, I'm a little bi-furious!"

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:38.320
Scott Pilgrim vs. the World marks&nbsp;
the second project that found Cera&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.880
and Whitman sharing the screen —&nbsp;
earlier, they starred together as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:45.520
George Michael Bluth and his unremarkable&nbsp;
girlfriend Ann on Arrested Development,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:50.080
roles that continued throughout the original&nbsp;
series as well as its belated Netflix revival.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:54.080
Though Whitman has appeared in movies like&nbsp;
2012's The Perks of Being a Wallflower and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:59.360
2015's The DUFF, most of her work has been on&nbsp;
television: she's had several guest roles and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:04.000
is one of the stars of NBC's crime comedy Good&nbsp;
Girls alongside Retta and Christina Hendricks.

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:10.160
At the start of Scott Pilgrim vs. the World, Scott&nbsp;
is utterly devoted to his role as the bassist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:15.120
of Sex Bob-omb, but as he gets more involved&nbsp;
with Ramona and his battles against her exes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:19.600
he ends up shirking his responsibilities.&nbsp;
Enter Young Neil, played by Johnny Simmons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:23.760
the meek and soft-spoken roadie who&nbsp;
follows the band around; a bassist himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:28.720
Neil knows all of Scott's parts, and ends up&nbsp;
filling in for him more or less permanently.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:32.880
Simmons had already popped up in Diablo&nbsp;
Cody's horror comedy Jennifer's Body and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.720
other recognizable films by the time he&nbsp;
appeared in Scott Pilgrim. In recent years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:42.480
Simmons has acted in movies like 21 Jump Street&nbsp;
and 2016's The Late Bloomer. He's also made guest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:47.280
appearances on television series and had a regular&nbsp;
role on Netflix's short-lived series Girlboss.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:53.760
Bill Hader might not physically appear in Scott&nbsp;
Pilgrim vs. the World, but if you listen carefully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:58.240
during a scene between Scott and Ramona, you&nbsp;
can clearly hear his distinctive voice. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:02.480
Ramona mentions that Scott's hair is getting&nbsp;
shaggy, he notes that he got his last haircut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:07.120
just a few hours before his bad breakup with&nbsp;
Envy; as he reminisces on their split, Hader's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:12.320
voice contradicts him, clarifying that Scott was&nbsp;
brutally dumped, no matter what he tells Ramona.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:14.960
"It was a mutual thing." "It wasn't." "I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:19.760
she told me it was mutual."&nbsp;
"She dumped him. It was brutal."

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:25.040
Hader was already a staple of Saturday Night&nbsp;
Live when he provided this cheeky voiceover,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:29.520
albeit toward the end of his tenure. Though Hader&nbsp;
is best known for comedic roles in movies like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:34.880
Trainwreck and Inside Out, the actor has taken&nbsp;
on more dramatic roles in recent years. In 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:40.800
he starred as an adult Richie in It: Chapter Two,&nbsp;
and beginning in 2018, he's played the title role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:45.600
on HBO's Barry as an assassin turned actor,&nbsp;
which has earned him multiple Emmy Awards.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:51.920
Every band needs a good-looking, guitar-playing&nbsp;
frontman, and in Sex Bob-omb, that frontman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:56.480
is Stephen Stills, played by Mark Webber.&nbsp;
Desperate for a record deal, Stephen will do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.480 --> 00:13:01.360
just about anything to launch the band to stardom,&nbsp;
including betraying Scott to sign with Gideon.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:05.840
After his turn as Stephen, Mark Webber showed&nbsp;
up in fare like For a Good Time, Call...,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:10.480
Laggies and Happy Christmas. Webber also&nbsp;
does plenty of work behind the camera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:13.120
working on some of films in multiple capacities:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:19.840
he wrote, directed, and starred in movies like&nbsp;
2014's The Ever After and 2017's Flesh and Blood.

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:24.400
At the beginning of Scott Pilgrim vs. the&nbsp;
World, Scott's friends berate him for dating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.240
a much younger girl — specifically, a&nbsp;
high school student named Knives Chau,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:32.400
played by Ellen Wong. Knives idolizes&nbsp;
Scott and can't believe her luck in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:37.280
dating an older man. Well… man-child.&nbsp;
She is absolutely obsessed with Scott,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:43.280
but as he starts to fall for Ramona, he pushes&nbsp;
Knives aside, inspiring her desire for revenge.

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:45.680
"I’m not talking to you! I'm talking to her!"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:52.800
"What" "You broke the heart that&nbsp;
broke mine. Get ready to chow down!"

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:57.520
Wong's wide-eyed demeanor and her previous martial&nbsp;
arts training helped her land the role of Knives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:01.120
and after Scott Pilgrim, she continued&nbsp;
working steadily on the small screen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:06.160
Wong has appeared in several hit television shows,&nbsp;
including The Carrie Diaries and Dark Matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:10.160
eventually landing a recurring role with&nbsp;
Netflix on their original series GLOW.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.760
Wong played the role of Jenny, who&nbsp;
wrestles under the moniker Fortune Cookie.

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:20.480
Scott Pilgrim vs. the World is full of hilarious&nbsp;
supporting players, few of whom are quite as funny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:26.080
as Michael Comeau, played by Nelson Franklin.&nbsp;
Comeau is absolutely everywhere, from the party&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:30.480
where Scott first meets Ramona to the Chaos&nbsp;
Theatre during Scott and Gideon's final battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:36.160
and no matter where he is, he can be heard in the&nbsp;
background making some sort of obnoxious comment.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:38.960
"You know, so I told them&nbsp;
you've got a really good sound,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:41.360
and I think you should market&nbsp;
your sound to deaf people."

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:46.640
Franklin, tends to pop up in television and&nbsp;
film projects as a utilitarian comedic actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:50.880
though television is where you've most likely&nbsp;
noticed him. He's appeared in recurring roles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:55.520
on some of the best comedies of the last&nbsp;
several years, including The Office, Veep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.520 --> 00:15:01.040
New Girl, and black-ish, and was a part of the&nbsp;
main cast on shows such as The Millers and Abby's.

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:06.880
Before Scott even learns about Ramona's seven&nbsp;
evil exes, he attends a Battle of the Bands with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:12.080
Sex Bob-omb — with both Ramona and Knives in the&nbsp;
audience — and finds himself in a very different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:16.880
kind of battle when Ramona's first ex, Matthew&nbsp;
Patel, played by Satya Bhabha, shows up and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:21.760
performs a Bollywood-style song and dance number&nbsp;
about fighting Scott. Scott makes pretty quick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:27.200
work of Matthew, but as a result of the fight,&nbsp;
Ramona is forced to explain the situation at hand.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:31.120
The British-born Bhabha appeared in the&nbsp;
leading role in 2012's Midnight's Children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:35.760
based on the novel of the same name, and followed&nbsp;
that up with recurring roles in comedies like New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:41.440
Girl and Eastsiders. More recently, from 2017 to&nbsp;
2018, Bhabha played the recurring role of Habib&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:46.240
in Netflix's original series Sense8, appearing&nbsp;
for five episodes throughout its second season.

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:51.280
Early on in Scott Pilgrim vs. the World, Sex&nbsp;
Bob-omb faces off against competitors in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:55.040
Battle of the Bands; unfortunately&nbsp;
for rival band Crash and the Boys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:59.920
Matthew Patel's arrival signals their doom.&nbsp;
Erik Knudsen plays leading man Crash and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:04.560
armed with their very own girl drummer — much&nbsp;
to Kim's chagrin, the band launches into their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:09.280
hits. After they're incinterated, though,&nbsp;
Sex Bob-omb wins the competition by default.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:14.480
A year after Scott Pilgrim, Knudsen showed up&nbsp;
in the 2011 horror sequel Scream 4. These days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:17.840
Knudsen is probably best known for&nbsp;
his recurring and leading roles in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:22.000
shows like the dystopian Jericho and&nbsp;
the science fiction series Continuum.

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:27.360
Though it se19ems as if Todd Ingram's vegan&nbsp;
lifestyle will overpower Scott completely during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:32.080
their fight over Ramona, Scott ultimately&nbsp;
defeats his rival with an unlikely weapon:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:34.080
coffee with a splash of milk.

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:37.040
"What are you talking about?" "You&nbsp;
just drank half and half baby."

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:42.720
Almost immediately, the Vegan Police, played&nbsp;
by Thomas Jane and Clifton Collins Jr.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:48.080
show up to investigate. As it turns out,&nbsp;
Todd has been transgressing a lot lately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:53.200
enjoying everything from gelato to chicken&nbsp;
parmesan. After the Vegan Police revoke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:58.160
Todd's vegan powers for his crimes, they&nbsp;
prance off, high-fiving exuberantly.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:02.880
If you're a fan of HBO's original programming,&nbsp;
you might remember Jane from his series Hung,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:06.640
which aired from 2009 to 2011, and&nbsp;
if you're into science fiction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:10.640
you've probably seen him recently in&nbsp;
a leading role on Syfy's The Expanse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:15.600
As for Collins Jr., he showed up in 2019's&nbsp;
Once Upon a Time... in Hollywood and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:20.400
Veronica Mars continuation that same year, and&nbsp;
Westworld fans will recognize him as Lawrence.

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:26.160
Wallace makes plenty of conquests during Scott&nbsp;
Pilgrim vs. the World, and as it happens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:29.200
one of them actually shares a&nbsp;
name with the movie's protagonist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:34.400
Since Wallace and the main Scott share a bed,&nbsp;
Lewis's character Other Scott ends up bonding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:38.640
with his counterpart, privy to the personal&nbsp;
details of his life and pursuit of Ramona.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:42.960
Lewis has had plenty of television guest&nbsp;
roles, including parts in Designated Survivor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:48.000
The Handmaid's Tale, and Suits. He typically&nbsp;
plays minor roles in both film and television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.680
but he did play a recurring role on&nbsp;
Arrow as the adult William Clayton.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.920
As Scott approaches Gideon's&nbsp;
new venue, the Chaos Theater,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.920 --> 00:18:00.720
to fight Ramona's final evil ex for her&nbsp;
heart, he comes across an apparent obstacle:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:05.280
the place seems pretty closely guarded at first&nbsp;
glance. However, when Scott actually interacts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:10.080
with the security guards — played by John Patrick&nbsp;
Amedori and Joe Dinicol — anything from the word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:15.120
"whatever" to just a grunt gets him into the&nbsp;
theater, and when Scott revisits the boss battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:19.120
he vanquishes the guards entirely,&nbsp;
leaving piles of coins in his wake.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:22.880
Outside of Scott Pilgrim, Amedori has&nbsp;
been in several huge television shows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:27.120
including a recurring role on the hit teen soap&nbsp;
Gossip Girl as one of Serena van der Woodsen's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:32.800
love interests. Amedori also scored a leading role&nbsp;
as Gabe in 2017 on Netflix's Dear White People.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:38.560
As for Dinicol, like so many other Scott Pilgrim&nbsp;
performers, he's known for a role on Arrow — in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:44.480
his case, as Rory Regan, or Ragman — as well&nbsp;
as guest appearances on many other shows.

